  "_comment": "Gledopto GL-C-201W effect library. Captured from live ESP<->MCU serial link. Two entries were flagged as malformed during capture and are excluded until verified.",
  "_format_note": "hex = 1 scene-ID byte + N frames of 13 bytes. Frame: [0] reserved/unused byte, ignored by the MCU in JUMP and FADE; keep 50 (0x32) or 70 (0x46) for the Tuya layout. [1] frame duration / hold time, the only working timer: JUMP 0..107 = (108 - byte) * 0.1035 s, 108 = fast strobe after ~32.7 s startup delay, 109..255 = wrapped 16-bit ms counter (65.536 s) giving 65.43..50.17 s; FADE period = (108 - byte) * 0.207 s with byte < 65 transition+hold, 65..85 continuous ramp, 86..107 fast overlap. [2] style 00=static 01=jump 02=fade 03=strobe/flash. [3:5] hue degrees 0-360, [5:7] saturation 0-1000, [7:9] RGB value/brightness 0-1000, [9:11] white brightness 0-1000, [11:13] white temperature 0-1000. The UI uses these experimentally confirmed roles; the older '4646 palette' reading was wrong.",
